# --- Bag.events (Task 34 Part E inventory example) ---
#
# The pickups are world actors the scene author places: an actor named
# `SwordPickup` / `PotionPickup` that a click raycast can hit. Clicking one puts
# its item in the player's bag, hides the pickup and refills the bag window, so a
# new slot appears the moment you pick something up.

when scene starts
  hide group bag
  fill grid BagGrid from my bag

when B is pressed
  show group bag
  fill grid BagGrid from my bag

when SwordPickup is clicked
  add Sword to my bag
  hide SwordPickup
  fill grid BagGrid from my bag

when PotionPickup is clicked
  add Potion to my bag
  hide PotionPickup
  fill grid BagGrid from my bag

when slot 1 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot1 to my SelectedItem

when slot 2 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot2 to my SelectedItem

when slot 3 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot3 to my SelectedItem

when slot 4 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot4 to my SelectedItem

when slot 5 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot5 to my SelectedItem

when slot 6 of grid BagGrid is clicked
  set my SelectedItem to my ClickedSlot
  set text of SelectedLabel to my SelectedItem
  set tooltip of BagGridSlot6 to my SelectedItem
